  "raw_text": "40\n\nBanhwi\n \n(1) (a/t:\n \nBangwi\n-\nmy\n,\nbh,lv\n)\n \n–\n \nThe plural person of the verb\n \nKaia\n \n(\nto be\n) is formed by using\n \nBanhwi\n \nfollowed by\nthe appropriately conjugated\n \nKaia\n \nverb. / La persona plural del verbo\n \nKaia\n \n(ser/estar) se forma usando\n \nBanhwi\n \nseguido\ndel verbo\n \nKaia\n \nadecuadamente conjugado.\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n: Sometimes this is written as one word.\n \n/ A veces esto se escribe como una palabra.\n \nEx/Ej:\n \nBanhwisa\n \ninstead of / en\n\nvez de\n \nBanhwi sa\n)\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nYang nani banhwi sna\n \n–\n \nwe are\n \n/ nosotros somos;\n \nMan nani banhwi sma\n \n–\n \nyou are\n \n/ ustedes son;\n \nWitin nani banhwi sa\n \n–\n\nthey are\n \n/ ellos son\n\nYang nani banhwi kapri\n \n–\n \nwe were\n \n/ éramos;\n \nMan nani banhwi kapram\n \n–\n \nyou were\n \n/ ustedes fueron;\n \nWitin nani banhwi\nkan\n \n–\n \nthey were\n \n/ ellos eran\n\nYang nani banhwi kamna\n \n–\n \nwe will be\n \n/ nosotros seremos;\n \nMan nani banhwi kama\n \n–\n \nyou will be\n \n/ ustedes serán;\n \nWitin nani\nbanhwi kabia\n \n–\n \nthey will be\n \n/ ellos serán\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\n(\nmy33\n):\n \nwitin nani pat ridi bangwi kan\n \n–\n \nthey were all ready\n \n/ todos estaban listos\n\n(\nmy51\n):\n \nkau pain bangwi kama\n \n–\n \nyou will be better\n \n/ ustedes serán mejores\n\n(\nmy59\n):\n \nwitin nani pana pana pramis daukan ban kaiara pana bangwi kaia\n \n–\n \nthey made a promise to each other to\nalways be friends\n \n/ se prometieron mutuamente ser siempre amigos\n\nBanhwi\n \n(2) (a/t:\n \nBangwi\n-\nmy\n,\nbh\n&\nlv\n)\n \n–\n \nPlural person present participle verbs are followed by\n \nBanhwi\n \nalong with the\nconjugated\n \nKaia\n \nverb.\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\n(\nmy60\n):\n \nmain kaiki bangwi kapri\n \n–\n \nwe were looking after\n \n/ nosotros estábamos cuidando\n\n...................\n\nBani\n \n–\n \nevery, every one, all\n \n/ cada, cada uno, todos\n\nKumi bani\n \n–\n \neach one\n \n/ cada uno\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYawan kumi bani dîa daukaia sa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhat must each one of us do?\n \n/ ¿Qué debe hacer cada uno de nosotros?)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nmwb-09/20\n):\n \nDîa pitka kat G\nȃ\nd ba yawan kumi bani ra main wan kaikisa?\n \n–\n \nTo what extent does God pay attention\nto us as individuals?\n \n/ Hasta qué grado está Dios pendiente de cada uno de nosotros (individualmente)?)\n\nPiu bani\n \n–\n \nalways, every time\n, all the time\n \n/\n \nsiempre,\n \ncada vez,\n \ntodo el tiempo\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n06/19\n):\n \nNahki sip sa piu bani kau pain nu takaia\n \nJehova dîa\n \nwant sa yawan dukiara?\n \n–\n \nHow are we able to\n\nalways be\n \ncoming to know\n/perceive\n \nbetter what Jehovah wants for us?\n \n/\n \n¿Cómo podemos llegar a saber/percibir mejor lo\n\nque Jehová quiere para nosotros?\n)\n\nTasba bani\n \n–\n \nall the earth\n \n/\n \ntoda la tierra\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nSins L\nâ\nka\n \n15:3\n):\n \nTasba bani ra, Dawan nakra b\nâ\nra sa\n \n–\n \nIn all the earth, God’s eyes are there\n \n/\n \nEn toda la tierra, los\n\nojos de Dios están ahí\n)\n\nBapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand something up, to stick, to establish, to institute, to found, to anchor, to install\n \n/ levantar algo,\npegar, establecer, instituir, fundar, anclar, instalar\n\nBapaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \na stand\n \n/\n \npie (de sost\né\nn), atril, perchero\n\nKiandil bapaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nlampstand\n \n/ candelabro\n\nBapanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething stood up, something established, something anchored, principle\n \n(\nlv\n)\n \n/ algo se puso de\npie, algo establecido, algo anclado, principio (\nlv\n)\n\nBapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand up to, to stand up for, to endure\n \n/ resistir, defender, aguantar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nvi,wqu-05/22\n):\n \nlila kat bapi buaia\n \n–\n \nto stay in the middle; to stay neutral\n \n/ permanecer\n \nen el medio; mantenerse\nneutral)\n\nBan bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto endure, to continue to endure, to continue to stand up to, to remain firm, to\nremain steadfast\n \n/ aguantar, continuar aguantando, continuar resistiendo, continuar defendiendo,\nmantenerse firme, permanecer firme\n\nBapi buanka l\nâ\nka\n \n(\nwqu\n-\n10/19\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nendurance\n \n/\n \naguante\n\nDutki bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto endure in a firm and strong way, to stand up to in a firm and strong way, to\nstand up for in a firm and strong way\n \n/\n \naguantar de manera firme y fuerte, resistir de manera firme y\nfuerte, defender de manera firme y fuerte\n\nKasak bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto remain firm and true, to remain steadfast and true, to remain faithful and true\n \n/\n\npermanecer firme y verdadero, permanecer firme y verdadero, permanecer fiel y verdadero\n\nMapara bapi buaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stand up against, to stand up to\n \n/ enfrentarse a",
